WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.457
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will know what is available,

00:00:05.457 --> 00:00:10.914
issued, and expiring. Unrecorded transfers and missing expiry dates make stock levels unreliable

00:00:10.914 --> 00:00:16.372
and replenishment harder to plan. We will explain the features, the setup decisions,

00:00:16.372 --> 00:00:19.730
and a practical way to check the result.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:25.024
Medical supplies are tracked by lot with expiry alerts, and turnout gear is

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:29.719
issued to members. Know what you have, where it is and what is

00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:34.413
about to expire. The examples in this series use a fictional department and

00:00:34.413 --> 00:00:36.580
are teaching scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:42.935
Inventory. Items, stock levels and storage locations. Add the supplies and equipment you

00:00:42.935 --> 00:00:48.689
track and where they are stored. Availability also depends on Inventory. Check access

00:00:48.689 --> 00:00:50.460
in the target department.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:57.715
Inventory counts, expiry and alerts. Counts, expiry dates and low-stock alerts. Set minimum

00:00:57.715 --> 00:01:04.370
levels and expiry alerts for critical supplies. Availability also depends on Inventory. Check

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.930
access in the target department.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:12.975
Inventory Status. What is on hand, running low or expiring. Decide which supplies

00:01:12.975 --> 00:01:18.419
and equipment are worth tracking and where they are stored. Availability also depends

00:01:18.419 --> 00:01:21.770
on Inventory. Check access in the target department.

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:28.255
Transfer Inventory. Move stock between locations. Decide which supplies and equipment are worth

00:01:28.255 --> 00:01:34.139
tracking and where they are stored. Availability also depends on Inventory. Check access

00:01:34.139 --> 00:01:35.950
in the target department.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:42.053
Issue Equipment. Issue equipment to members and record returns. Decide which supplies and

00:01:42.053 --> 00:01:47.557
equipment are worth tracking and where they are stored. Availability also depends on

00:01:47.557 --> 00:01:50.520
Inventory. Check access in the target department.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:57.276
Inventory purchasing. Suppliers, purchase orders and deliveries. Decide which supplies and equipment are

00:01:57.276 --> 00:02:03.432
worth tracking and where they are stored. Availability also depends on Inventory. Check

00:02:03.432 --> 00:02:05.800
access in the target department.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:12.724
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Define the stock

00:02:12.724 --> 00:02:19.047
locations and items the department will track. Step 2. Record a receipt, transfer,

00:02:19.047 --> 00:02:25.371
and equipment issue using sample stock. Step 3. Review counts, expiry, low-stock alerts,

00:02:25.371 --> 00:02:26.830
and purchasing needs.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:33.085
Now verify the result. Reconcile a physical demo count with recorded stock. Check

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:38.740
the destination of a transfer, the equipment assignee, and the expiry record. A

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:44.395
common problem to watch for: A purchase order is distinct from a received

00:02:44.395 --> 00:02:48.310
delivery. Reconcile the receipt before assuming stock is available.

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:54.405
Your practice task is simple. Receive ten demo supplies, transfer two, and issue

00:02:54.405 --> 00:02:59.900
one durable item. Reconcile the resulting balances and inspect expiry alerts. Record the

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:05.396
result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use the

00:03:05.396 --> 00:03:09.200
linked feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

